 "youtube": {
  "title": "Gunpowder Plot: How Did One Letter Stop It?",
  "description": "The Gunpowder Plot almost blew up King James I and the whole House of Lords in 1605. So why does Britain light bonfires every 5 November? Because of one unsigned letter.\n\nPlotters rented the cellar under the House of Lords and hid 36 barrels of gunpowder there for the State Opening of Parliament on 5 November. Ten days before, Lord Monteagle got an anonymous letter warning of \"a terrible blow\", and he took it to the government. Near midnight, guards searched the undercroft and caught Guy Fawkes with the powder. Remember, remember the fifth of November: that is why Bonfire Night exists.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a true story like this every day. Who do you think wrote the Monteagle letter? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #gunpowderplot #bonfirenight #stickstory",
